  "text": "A procedure is presented for turning a type of spatially extended field, whose mutual influence can be described by equations that involve integrals, into a quantum description. Using a particular established approach, the authors build the operator that connects initial and final states of particle interactions. The resulting framework does not suffer from the usual problems of divergent series that plague many similar theories. It turns out that the model can be made to obey either a symmetry‑like rule that relates forward and backward processes, or a rule that ensures agreement with classical predictions in the appropriate limit, but it appears impossible to satisfy both requirements at the same time."
